\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0 >Osha (as in ocean) imagined the man lying beside her was her husband. But the oaf snoring away in her hammock, Fasho (as in asshole), was not it. His sweaty, deep-brown skin glistering in high-Sol through her window made her extra gushy, sure. But he was also brainless. And worthless.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 I like to start sentences with And and But as much as anyone, but they have to be measured out.  3/5 sentences starting with \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91but\u8217\'92 or \u8216\'91and\u8217\'92, in the first paragraph, is maybe too much. The writing begins to feel half-baked. You could drop the first \u8216\'91but\u8217\'92 and you would lose nothing.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 As I read on, this leads to a note on the style of the prose: there is a *lot* of \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91sure\u8217\'92, \u8216\'91well,\u8217\'92 \u8216\'91but,\u8217\'92 \u8216\'91and,\u8217\'92 etc. It\u8217\'92s \u8216\'91voicey\u8217\'92 writing, but it\u8217\'92s the first reflex when trying to write something voicey. I suggest trying to push past it and find something more unique and engaging. It\u8217\'92s difficult, but rewarding if you can figure it out. There\u8217\'92s always the option of just pruning this stuff (with some fiddling), because, imo, it isn\u8217\'92t actually elevating the prose.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 For example, I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92ve seen the following construction a jillion times: \u8220\'93x, sure. But y. And z\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 >extra gushy, sure. But he was also brainless. And worthless.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 It\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s AI-esque. For the rest, I\u8217\'92m just going to bold the bits I\u8217\'92m referring to:}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 >None of that mattered today,** though.** }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 > **Well, sure** the Tenente'd return her sister in exchange.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 >**Of course,** all natural islanders possessed }
\par\plain 
\par\plain {>**That, and the fact he was**}
\par\plain 
\par\plain {>**}{\f0\fs24\b0 Not that she hadn't** made a sincere effort.}{ }
\par\plain 
\par\plain {>Or use it, **more like**.}
\par\plain 
\par\plain {All this stuff disappears when you get to the dialog and the action.}
\par\plain 
\par\plain {___}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 > None of that mattered today, though. Because today was *the* day. Asha was coming home.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92m not a fan of vague allusions to why someone is excited to wake up in the morning. Honestly, I end up confused. Now, keep in mind I only got 3 hrs of sleep last night, but it wasn\u8217\'92t enjoyable trying to puzzle out the relationships between the characters when it felt like narrative was *trying* clarify all that for me early. It reads like this to me: Osha misses her husband (who is away? Or, does she just wish she was married and never was? Maybe he\u8217\'92s dead?). She\u8217\'92s cheating on her husband with Fasho (Maybe this is a permissive culture, idk. Not trying to be dense here; was genuinely confused). She\u8217\'92s excited because Asha (Who? her husband?) is coming home.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 It could be that I would have read this differently if I had read ch.1.  But aside from all that, the whole, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91none of that mattered today, though, because today was the day\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 is not a great hook. It\u8217\'92s just so\u8230\'85cliche.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Today was *the* day\u8221\'94\u8230\'85 come onnnnnn.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 >}{\f0\fs24\b0 O}{\f0\fs24\b0 sha sat up, resting her nagging feet on the bamboo floor. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91Nagging feet\u8217\'92? Why, after doing whatever she was doing in bed, does she need to rest her feet on the floor?  Were they doing a bunch of foot stuff? }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 >}{\f0\fs24\b0 B}{\f0\fs24\b0 rushing the dead serpents aside, she crossed the room and pulled her red leadership gown over her thickly nude body.}{ }
\par\plain 
\par\plain {I don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know what a \u8216\'91leadership gown\u8217\'92 is, or what it looks like. Cannot picture it in my minds eye. Nor do I know how she feels about it, which may (or may not?) be important. And whatever she\u8217\'92s doing with the \u8216\'91herb clippings and snake tissue\u8217\'92 is entirely unclear, and not in a mysterious way.}
\par\plain 
\par\plain {>}{\f0\fs24\b0 E}{\f0\fs24\b0 verything she touched turned to shite. As though she were Midas's tethered.}
\par\plain 
\par\plain {Tethered means attached by a rope (or chain). I don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know how you\u8217\'92re interpreting that as something like \u8216\'91an inverse midas touch\u8217\'92. Again, only 3 hrs of sleep here, so maybe I\u8217\'92m just missing it. Anyways, the \u8216\'91as though she were\u8217\'92 is clunky as hell, perhaps shows you don\u8217\'92t trust the \u8216\'91Midas\u8217\'92s tethered\u8217\'92 bit. I think whatever you put there should be so clear enough that you wouldn\u8217\'92t need to remind the reader that the figurative speech is referring to her.}
\par\plain 
\par\plain {>F}{\f0\fs24\b0 l}{\f0\fs24\b0 agship Tenente Grantchev (as in pants off), came in person from New Clear Water City. Allegedly speaking for some foreigners who'd inquired about an antivenin\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85}{\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93}{\f0\fs24\b0 Hell yes, sir. I'll do it right away."}{\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85}{\f0\fs24\b0 .}{\f0\fs24\b0 T}{\f0\fs24\b0 hen she made no progress.\~ When the offworlders discovered the truth, they'd kill her. Maybe everyone. She didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know and didn\u8217\'92t want to think too long on it.}{ }
\par\plain 
\par\plain {There\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s some weird tense shenanigans going on. The \u8216\'91then\u8217\'92 in \u8216\'91Then she made no progress\u8217\'92 is continuing a narrative that occurred in the past, but is referring to the present, and next, the future.}
\par\plain 
\par\plain {>Of course, all natural islanders possessed some resistance to the Yellow Rot. Hers was only slightly better than most. Not that she hadn't made a sincere effort. But after two revs, she'd grown  no closer to isolating the molecule that granted her partial-immunity..}
\par\plain 
\par\plain {This is an info dump without the dump. I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92m fine with \u8216\'91telling\u8217\'92 over showing, so long as the telling is interesting (e.g. the opening of the tale of two cities). But here it\u8217\'92s like, you\u8217\'92re sneaking in an info dump, but it\u8217\'92s minimally informative, and comes out of fucking nowhere. It\u8217\'92s not at all clear what any of it has to do with what has come before.}
\par\plain 
\par\plain 
\par\plain {Lastly, a very subjective opinion. I do not like or believe Osha. A woman who is banging every man in sight is not mourning her husband. I do not mean to invalidate whatever you may or may not be experiencing, but there are two widows in my life who loved their husbands very much and they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re still not \u8216\'91out and about\u8217\'92, even after a decade or so and a significant amount of therapy. I know everyone is different, but, that\u8217\'92s my take. Again, I apologize if it came of as invalidating.}
\par\plain 
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha sat up, resting her nagging feet on the bamboo floor. Dozens of golden-brown and blackened viper carcasses dangled from vines spanning her octagonal tree house. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Brushing the dead serpents aside, she crossed the room and pulled her red leadership gown over her thickly nude body. She picked at the tight knots in her unruly coils of hair, but soon gave up in frustration. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 The kitchen area was a catastrophe. Herb clippings and snake tissue coated each surface. She scooped up the larger chunks by hand and threw them in the redclay bucket. "Damnit all to the night, I hate myself." Everything she touched turned to shite. As though she were Midas's tethered. Twenty and eight revs; lonely and loveless. So many wrinkles. And so few teeth.  A wasted life of nothing but sacrifice. Everything for her sister. Everything. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91Lies have short legs, anzhinya.\u8217\'92 Her Yay\u225\'E1. The old bitch flittered about behind Osha\u8217\'92s eyelids, haranguing her as she'd done when alive. \u8216\'91Mentirosa! Mentirosa!'}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha was no mentirosa. Sometimes people just respond how they think others expect them to. Flagship Tenente Grantchev (as in pants off), came in person from New Clear Water City. Allegedly speaking for some foreigners who'd inquired about an antivenin. Could she possibly make one for them? Well, sure the Tenente'd return her sister in exchange. Only one answer existed. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hell yes, sir. I'll do it right away."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Then she made no progress.  When the offworlders discovered the truth, they'd kill her. Maybe everyone. She didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know and didn\u8217\'92t want to think too long on it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Kneeling, Osha sweeped up slices of viper and herbs. She\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d fry them tonight to spice the supperstew. The gelatinous parts, she dumped in the redclay bucket along with the bigger chunks. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Of course, all natural islanders possessed some resistance to the Yellow Rot. Hers was only slightly better than most. Not that she hadn't made a sincere effort. But after two revs, she'd grown  no closer to isolating the molecule that granted her partial-immunity..}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 She bent to pick up a stray snakeskin, and something bit her ass. Bad.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Damn, baby.\u8221\'94 Never mind. It was only Fasho. \u8220\'93Lookit that fat bunda jiggle.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Poxa vida, Fash,\u8221\'94 she said. \u8220\'93You scared the shit outta me. Don\u8217\'92t sneak up like that, man." }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Barely a man. He'd seduced her weeks ago with his crooked smile and dark, laughing eyes. That, and the fact he was the only person with a dick this side of the Torre. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I was only admirin that juicy ass, baby.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Watch that \u8216\'91baby\u8217\'92 shite."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oi, oi. I hear ya, Mam\u227\'E3e.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 She dreaded the humiliation were any of her mulyeres to drop by and see the cooking area right then. The girls were always visiting to admire her iron stove\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the only one in Mam\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u227\'E3e's Treetops. Or use it, more like. That wouldn\u8217\'92t do. She doubted she\u8217\'92d be alive this time tomorrow. But some things you don\u8217\'92t compromise. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Fasho made himself known again. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oi. You wanna hear one funny joke?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nope.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sonya (as in bone ya) she say you got a butter-bod.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93A snappin piranha's what she is. I told you to be wakeful with that one. Go on then. What\u8217\'92s a butter bod?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She say you gotta pretty face, but your body is so fat. Like butter! Get it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha rolled her eyes. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I think perhaps you misunderstood the joke, meu amor.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I tell her, \u8216\'91Oi, skank. Osh, she got twenty n three whole teeth. All her own. N Sonya standin there with only twelve.\u8221\'94 Fasho smirked. \u8220\'93Plus that face, Mam\u227\'E3e," he said, snickering. "Feia muita."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No it ain\u8217\'92t,\u8221\'94 Osha said. \u8220\'93She\u8217\'92s a very pretty young lady. Just est\u250\'FApida. Like you.\u8221\'94 She gathered up the salvageable cilantro and mint remnants. \u8220\'93Anywise, you can't ruin it for me today, little doggy. Not today, you won't. Oh my stars! Just thinkin on it. Just one rote more. Or maybe even tonight n Asha'll  be here. Home. Where she belongs.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Fasho reached into the redclay bowl on Osha's table, grabbed himself a big clawful of mamay-fruit jerky, and crammed it into his fat gob, talking while he chewed, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mayhap. We see. Be nice to have her back.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 "The things that pervertido's been doin to her. My baby sister, chained to his bed for revs and revs. Only a child. May his death be o so slow and painful.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 She smiled a sinister but satisfied smile, whispering, \u8220\'93Eu so queria poder ver."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Fasho dressed himself in his orange middle-management gown and sat on the floor beside her as she cleaned. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Easy, baby. All that chained to a bed nonsense ain't but women's gossip. Didn't nobody chain the girl to no bed. Look. The Pow's an asshole. Everybody say so. But Asha ain't no child no more. Anywise, ya don\u8217\'92t gotta go on about it all day."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha scoured the floor, raising her sponge, then slamming it down with each syllable she spoke, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, thank you for the pep talk, Fash.When'd you grow such a love for the Pedros? From do nada, eh? Ugh! You causa me desgosto.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Heyyy. What\u8217\'92s all this?\u8221\'94 Fasho caressed her shoulder. She shrugged him off.  \u8220\'93Everythin OK with the\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 uh, situation?\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha considered telling him the truth. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Of course.\u8221\'94 Changed her mind. \u8220\'93Just heavy-hearted is all. Missing my Marlo (as in Marlo).\u8221\'94 She shuddered and snorted, and blew hard into her old green snotrag.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hey, it's no worries, Mam\u227\'E3e. Five revs ain't shit. I could serve em with a fat pau in my no cu."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 She tried to smile at his joke. "He's dead. We both know it. Gods, I can't stand myself no more. And why in the night am I telling you this, anywise?"}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well mayhaps ya'd feel better by doin somethin, eh. Get offa that fat bunda and help out with the harvest. Eat a little less, maybe? Or go on a hike.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s nothin, Fash. Just jittery at the last minute. A few administrative things I gotta deal with.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Ignoring her, he continued, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Trim that natty mess of hair.\u8221\'94 He cackled like he thought that last was hilarious. \u8220\'93Get after that shaggy bush while you at it. Try smiling once in a while. Hell, anything other than mope around about your sister all the day.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You weren\u8217\'92t complainin about my hairy snatch this morning, was ya. Matter fact, ya got so excited, ya come apart in me fore I even got started.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Can't be helped, Mamae. That big, blubbery ass drive me crazy. Baby.\u8221\'94 He smacked her ass. Again.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s jaw clenched so tightly, she feared she'd break one of her twenty n three teeth. \u8220\'93You vile pau no cu! I told you n I told you about callin me baby.\u8221\'94 She seized the red bucketful of snake offal, reared back like a rockball pitcher, and hucked the revolting contents all over Fash. \u8220\'93Din I, puta?"}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Jellied meat-syrup dripped from his face down to the floor, and wet hunks of scale and bone clung to his gown. She spat in his face, and it merged with the slime already dripping from his suck-ass nose. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Fasho held his hands up, surrendering. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Forgive me, Mam\u227\'E3e. I won't do it again.\u8221\'94  He trudged over to the washing area to clean the ick from himself.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha kneeled to clean the ick from the floor. "You forget yourself too easily. Just cause you\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re the only man in the troop, doesn't mean I won\u8217\'92t chuck you out."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I doubt that. Not yet, ya  won't, anywise. Cause factually, I got something you're gonna wanna know about.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93More lies.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Not this time, Mam\u227\'E3e. No whaleshit, promise.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Spit."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Fasho finished up washing and sacheted bare-assed to the open window to air dry. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The gate warden reported that 'she' stopped by again last night.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha's whole body buzzed with that buzzy kind of anxiety.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Who did? The offworlders? Surely not.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Naw, Mam\u227\'E3e. The Princ\u233\'E9ss! Pharaoh\u8217\'92s daughter. With all the flesh on, as they say. Supposably, anywise. On some crazy shit. Visions, the gods are angry, all kindsa alien beins n whatnot, the neo-Revelation, blah, blah.\u8221\'94 He crossed back to the hammock and occupied it. "The night gatewarden, she write it all down for ya. Happ'nin today, if ya can believe it.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 What he don't know. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Seriamente? Did anyone actually see 'Her Majesty'?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Naw, but she was certain. Same tall, skinny bitch, covered all in green, hiding in the trees like before.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha's back ache returned. She lay down, joining Fasho in the hammock. Draping her thigh over his crotch, she slung her arm across his chest, twirling that thatch of hairs with her finger. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Who was on-gate last night?" she purred. "It was Thresha (as in Ke$ha), I'd wager.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Fasho demurred, then held her so close, and kissed her deeply. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Naw," he admitted. "It was Sonya."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha shot from amorous to furious quick as a lancehead. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I knew it, you duplicitous godsdamned\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 " And shoved him hard. Fasho fell from hammock to floor, landing on his ass. \u8220\'93Take that skank off-gate immediately. I don't care why. Cite security reasons. Put her on nightsoil for the next three cycles.\u8221\'94 She paused for a moment to think.  \u8220\'93A-and she takes over the midden-dump from Thresha."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Fasho rose to his knees, massaging his ass. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Aw, c'mon baby. She do OK when she tries.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha sat up, finger in his face. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93\u8216\'91Baby\u8217\'92, my ass. You fodendo her? You are, ain't ya?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hell naw I ain\u8217\'92t fuck her, baby.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Call me \u8216\'91fuckin baby\u8217\'92 one more time. See what happens. Do it. I wish you would. Puta.\u8221\'94  And she spat in his face again. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, factually, I ain\u8217\'92t zactly call ya fuckin baby," said Fasho, progressing toward an enraged roar. \u8220\'93I called ya baby. Baby." The normous man stood, flashing a hateful sneer down at her, mouthing the words, 'Fuckin baby.'}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha stood also, turned, stomped toward the floor-hatch, and prised it open, showing him the fifteen-meter drop below. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Out."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Shoulders slumped, Fasho exhaled loud and long and went to climb down the ladder. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No ya don\u8217\'92t, puta. No ladder for you.\u8221\'94 The dejected man climbed back up. \u8221\'94Jump."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Fasho opened his mouth to speak, and she smacked him. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are ya deaf, Est\u250\'FApido? Me deesay \u8216\'91jump'!\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 The man stiffened, all wet-eyed, and Osha sidled behind him, tickling his nape with her breath. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Shh. You low-life cuzow. Make one sound," she said, trailing warm air down his spine, ever so slowly, puffing softly. "Just one." }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 His lip quivered and the soft tears flowed, quiet as a slashed artery. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 "And I push." She pressed her heavy body against his, gradually increasing the pressure until his fungussy-thick yellow toetips were the only things standing between him and a tumbling death. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Fasho squinted. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I do love you, ya know. In my way.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Jump.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s ears filled then, and the air was heavy. A deafening silence followed, like the sort just before a cyclone lands. A single blast erupted. Moments later, a hammering concussion ripped through her hut, knocking the unlikely lovers backward. All her things: plates and cups, snake-curtains, herbs, artwork, and lanterns, the redclay bowl her sister had made for her wedding, along with all the mamey-jerky inside it, plus an eighth of the roof, all crashed to the floor. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Then another blast force ricocheted through the shuddering hut. And another, and another, and another. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Hugging Osha to him, Fasho grasped the central support pole, dragging her away from the lethal drop downward. The pair sheltered in a corner, firmly embraced, waiting for the barrage to end. But it didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t end. Not for a long, long time. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 The little tree hut spasmed on its supports. Her prized iron stove slid across the floor, threatening to burst through the sagging south wall.  Choppy whines and percussive bangs swelled in a hellish chorus. The squeals of her dying enemies carried downwind, and she beamed. The offworlders had fulfilled one part of the treaty, at least. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 From a kilometer away, the battle delivered heavy black smoke in gusts that billowed in through the open windows.  Burnt oil stink and scorched flesh stench filled the hut, overwhelming them both. Fasho coughed and hacked. Had a convulsive fit. Lost consciousness. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Osha grasped his wrists and tugged, intending to drag him to the hatch. Instead, she stumbled backward, and nearly out the lethal door. She was strong. But this dope weighed a metric ton. Wrapping her arms around his neck, she pulled. He stopped choking then. Hell, he stopped breathing.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 She scanned about for some kind of indeterminate something. Anything to rescue her from this lousy predicament. Mayhap the \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91snake curtain\u8217\'92 was long enough. She wrapped one end round the support post. Hitched off a serviceable bowline. Fastened the other end round Fasho. Thrice wrapped his shoulders. The drop was fifteen meters. Sixteen tops.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 She pulled her walking boots on, and, bracing her body against the post, pushed Fasho with her soles. One centimeter at a time, she chucked him out. Just how she said she was gonna. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 The big man dropped and snagged about four meters shy of the ground. He screamed bloody agony, both shoulders surely subluxed. At least he was breathing again.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 She snapped up her dagger, stuck the handle in her mouth, and started her own descent. Seven rungs down, she looked at the ground. It breathed at her. Fifty, sixty kilometers tops. Another concussion slammed the village, and Osha fell straight down. Her last thought was,  \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91Gods, what an ignoble and surprising end.\u8217\'92}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 But then Fasho had her. In his normous arms, he held her tight. And somehow he had her. She caught her breath for a moment, then pecked his cheek, and thanked the man. Reaching back, she scrabbled to grasp a rung, and swung herself back onto the ladder.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Poor Fasho. Dangling there like a sticky turd refusing to detach. Sawing with her knife, she cut the vine holding him in suspension. He fell and hit the ground. A sickening crunch reported back. Unnerved, Osha hissed and reflex-jerked her own leg upward. She nearly slid down the tree, keen to see if Fasho was alive. He was. Though his leg was propped unnaturally, and he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d likely be screaming once he woke. Kneeling beside him, she said, \u8220\'93You were really gonna do it, weren't ya, puta?\u8221\'94 Ugh. Empathy is such a waste of mind space. She kissed his cheek and whispered, \u8220\'93I do hope you'll be OK. I'll send the girls.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 She moved on to damage assessment and triage. The other mulyeres and meninas needed to be rounded up, and any casualties counted. Visibility, though, was nil; and the chokey black smoke swirled all about her, enshrouding the treetop village. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mam\u227\'E3e Osha! Mam\u227\'E3e Osha!\u8221\'94 The black cloud shat out Sonya\u8217\'92s worthless ass, screeching as she ran nearer. The rotten little whore. Fasho's exact type, though. Light skinneded. Perfect facial structure, in spite of her dental scarcity. Beaded box-braids. Slutty puta prolly works on them when she's supposed to be on the godsdamned gate.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Sonya stopped just short of running her over, and Osha palmed the girl's face. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Fetch the mulyeres and meninas," she said.  "Everyone. Code Yellow.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But Mam\u227\'E3e\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 "}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Quieto,\u8221\'94 she shouted, overpowered by sounds of screeching metal and whistling missiles. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93When do I say for?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Ahora,\u8221\'94 Osha said, tapping her pointer finger to the ground. \u8220\'93Now. If it ain't too much trouble for ya.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 "No ma\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92am.  Is just that\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 "}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0  \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Say to carry Fasho with em. Now get to running, fool."}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0}